WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.560
78th Annual Harvest Festival Last Night Event

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.240
Soybean 
Burgers

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.280
And it's healthy! 
Super healthy! No, really...

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.280
Boiled Gyoza

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.280
Soybean Juice

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.790
Grilled 
Daikon

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.710
Wow, so many of the 
stalls have moved here.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.580
Oh, and it's all free of charge now.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.400
How about some yakisoba?

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.300
Everything that didn't sell out is 
dinner for the students tonight.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.840
Eat some 
and think of 
it as helping 
us out!

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.430
Soybean 
Sandwiches

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.970
The goal of the harvest festival 
is to leave nothing behind,

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.560
so the stalls with food leftover 
have to stay open tonight.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:43.060
10.5x 
Soy 
Flour

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:43.060
We've got 
too much 
leftover!!

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:43.060
Please help! We want to go home!

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.940
Medieval Europe Research Club
Grilled Foods

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.190
To guys like us who have 
been after the prize,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.650
they're the losers.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.070
But every year,

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.030
there aren't many stalls selling 
anything that tastes bad.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.040
<i>I will now announce the</i>

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.200
<i>stall that placed third in 
the top sellers ranking!</i>

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.540
<i>Of the many stalls this year...</i>

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.960
So anyway, use this money if you want.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.960
<i>our third place winner drew out the 
value of soybeans to the fullest,</i>

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.340
<i>and sold out its product 
within three hours!</i>

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.180
You guys were thinking 
of Haruka-san, too?

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:19.680
<i>The Agricultural Technology Research 
Team's "Soybean Bento" stall!</i>

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.180
Well...

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.310
And here I am, dressed like 
this for my own gains...

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.350
Well...

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.540
<i>Congratulations to the 3rd place team!</i>

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.100
Hey, no matter how it turns out,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.400
you were still great as a woman.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.920
<i>They will be awarded a special prize 
of a year's worth of soybeans!</i>

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.900
Is this really okay?

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.400
Am <i>I</i> really okay?

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.700
Even if our stall only wins 
because of Oikawa and Yuuki...

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.950
Uh... you should be proud, too!

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.870
Sawaki, want to eat this?

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.870
It's a beef offal bowl.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.620
Sure.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.290
The stall this came from served 
beef dishes during the day,

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:53.630
and they had decided to serve 
the offal dishes at night.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.720
So they planned to be open 
tonight from the start.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.550
If you look around, there are 
a lot of stalls like that.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.510
This school is amazing.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.660
<i>Moving on, I will now 
announce the second place stall!</i>

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.220
All these people with different goals,

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.730
Food Stall 
Awards Ceremony

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.100
supporting each other and 
having fun together.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.960
<i>This team's steadfast work ethic set them apart.</i>

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:11.230
Maybe I was right to enter this school.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.230
<i>And the flavor of their product would 
move any Japanese person's heart!</i>

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:17.510
<i>The Plant Nutrition Research Team's "Sticky Rice 
with Autumn Wild Vegetables Bento" stall!</i>

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.860
It's not exactly glitzy, 
and it's sort of dorky,

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.570
but I think I'll be able to 
enjoy the Tokyo campus life

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.030
Sawaki-kun talked about.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:29.500
Moyashimon

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.500
Returns

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:57.440
Host

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.460
And now for the announcement 
of the first place food stall!

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.050
Oh, here it comes!

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.960
It's gotta be Mutou-san's 
stall this year.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.630
A bunny with a gothic lolita... 
that's playing dirty!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.470
Even I went to take a picture...

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.970
The wait is over!

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:12.230
Are you all ready for this?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:12.230
So, who's going to go to France, anyway?

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.940
It should be you, obviously.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:18.730
The time has come to weed out the many powerful contenders

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.730
What? But I just came back 
to Japan in the spring...

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.400
There's no way I'm going.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:23.030
and carve a new name in the glorious history of our harvest festival!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.030
I actually don't do well on airplanes.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.160
I don't think I'm up 
to such a huge task.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.160
I will now announce the winner!

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:33.980
Host

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:34.540
The stall that ranked first in 
popularity with visitors and students

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.500
as well as in profits,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.010
hailed as the most straightforward 
representation of our school's spirit...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:42.800
Come on!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.760
The Livestock Department's 
Fried Chicken!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.810
What?!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.060
Bullshit!

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.020
Our stall had the most customers by far!

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:58.020
By the way, Aoi's Bar, the stall with 
the highest profits and popularity,

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.000
Host

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.230
was suspected of using the school's

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.650
memorial tree in making its product,

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.650
and when we checked with 
the Itsuki seminar...

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.610
<i>I'm sure they did.</i>

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.160
...was Professor Itsuki's confirmation.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.160
Thus, they forfeit their prize money.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.540
The two second-years 
who led the operation

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.290
will be suspended from 
school for 20 days.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.300
Stupid Stupid Stupid Stupid Stupid Stupid

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.210
They're done for! \ (^o^) /

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.300
Idiots Idiots Idiots

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.800
What was that about?!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.800
Oh, really?

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.390
You've been suspended?

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.640
Why couldn't you just 
pretend you didn't know?!

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.970
I guess it can't be helped.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.100
Well, this seems like a good

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.810
chance to ask a favor, 
Misato-kun and Kawahama-kun.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.360
I'd like you to buy some 
wine and cheese for me.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.070
What?!

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.700
Well, I asked Hasegawa-kun to do it,

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.200
but she took off, you know?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.620
You there, boy...

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.950
Come here.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.250
Have you seen Haruka?

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.800
She hasn't been here at all lately.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.130
She's been raising us,

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.050
and we want her to check 
that we're doing okay.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.260
There are a lot of yeasts here.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.720
Looks like most of them 
are for refined sake.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.350
Yeah.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.520
Hasegawa-san was cultivating

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.980
all kinds of yeasts for 
the fermenting cellar.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:22.980
Male

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:22.980
Female

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.980
Mutou

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.980
Oikawa

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.280
And my recommended 
marketplace is right here.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.760
There's this plaza called 
something or other...

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:34.200
Wait, wait, wait!

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.250
Why is it in France?!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.460
Well, when you think of cheese and wine,

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.250
what else comes to mind but France?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:42.630
Is this about Hasegawa?!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:44.750
Why do we have to go?!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.760
Misato-san, Kawahama-san...

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.760
Hey, Sawaki! 
Say something to this old geezer!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:51.510
Tell him!

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.260
Let's go to France.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.720
What?!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.310
There's still a lot I want 
to learn from Hasegawa-san.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.030
Look, I've got three tickets.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.240
You're such a fool, Tadayasu.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:17.410
Overseas Travel Checklist

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.200
You really are stupid, Tadayasu.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.620
France

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:23.000
You can't go overseas without 
soy sauce and miso, can you?

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:27.670
How could a pushover like you 
ignore your theory so easily?

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.590
Shut up!

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:31.630
Why would I need miso and soy sauce 
when I'm only going for a few days?!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.050
Don't underestimate the 
adaptability of a teenager!

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.350
You don't understand anything.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.810
Don't underestimate the sudden 
bouts of homesickness

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.390
that strike when you're overseas.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.780
Fine.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:52.240
Also, why am I losing a war 
of words with these guys?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.280
Yay!

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.250
There's a temple or 
something right in the

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.330
middle of the Route des 
Grand Crus in Burgundy...

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.800
They've reserved it for the 
civil wedding ceremony.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.340
Haruka-san and her fiancé

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.970
are staying in the Imperial 
Suite at the Ritz Paris.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.760
According to the professor, 
if we want to find her,

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.810
one of those two would 
be the place to start.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.640
Why are you two the ones to see us off?

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.810
Because we were the only ones 
with nothing else to do today.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:25.980
Aida Makoto.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:26.480
Here.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.820
Itou Miyuki.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:28.190
Here.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.360
Oikawa Hazuki.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.030
Here.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.070
Kikuhara Shinji.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:31.570
Here.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.070
Sawaki Tadayasu.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.320
Here.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.990
Sawaki?

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.870
Yes.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.620
You sound weak.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:43.830
Yes!

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.840
To The Three Of You

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.840
Take care. 
-Yuuki Kei

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.840
See ya! -Mutou

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.840
Bring me a 
souvenir! 
-Oikawa

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.840
Itsuki 
Keizou

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.840
Also, I brought these 
messages from all of us.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.480
You shouldn't have.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.340
Wow, that's a 787!

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.670
Good luck, Sawaki-kun.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.590
It's second sons that make the 
world go 'round, you know.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.340
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:58.760
Just the bias of an

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:02.270
eldest daughter who's expected 
to live a conscientious life.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.860
Well, actually, second 
sons just stir things up.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.780
You should stir things 
up now and then, too.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:16.990
And when you get back, bring the 
princess and everyone else to my bar.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.370
Sure.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.200
Bye!

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.870
Good luck!

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.960
I bet Haruka-san will be surprised

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.880
when those three show 
up to bring her home.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.880
She tends to not realize

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.720
how important she is to 
the people around her.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.260
You may be right.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:46.390
Hotel Ritz Paris

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.990
You can't see the stars here, 
just like in Tokyo...

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.700
Attention, please!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:06.910
We're here in the airplane that 
has just departed from Narita.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:10.330
We microbes will be reporting 
freely from the boring,

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.920
confined hell that is economy class.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.930
But, wow, there are so many 
microbes in this plane!

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.600
I'm traveling around America and Japan.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.100
Stay away from the ducts!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.520
You'll get ventilated!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.600
Isn't there any soil in here?

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.310
The seats are too clean!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.730
Cling to a human!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:32.360
Fermentation is big in France, too.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.980
Try not to get a stomach ache in France.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.990
All right, let's brew 'til we drop!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:38.950
Shut up!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.410
Fermenting Cellar

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:43.700
There.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.370
Sorry to make you do all that.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.870
I just can't get moving today, again.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.710
This is no problem.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.420
Filling in for Sawaki-kun 
was way harder.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.460
Still, working the fermenting cellar

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.840
is pretty hard without any guys around.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.470
We're fine as long as 
you're here, Hazuki-chan.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.970
The guys never do any work, anyway.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:10.230
Sawaki-kun really impressed 
me this time, though.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.480
Taking the lead with Misato-kun 
and Kawahama-kun like that...

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.650
Yeah, when he first started here,

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.480
he just stuck to Yuuki-kun all the time.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:20.360
Since Yuuki-kun took leave from school,

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.700
he's been totally at the 
mercy of those two guys.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.870
I guess the first-year 
has grown up, huh?

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:31.870
And you spend all your days 
drowning in sake lately.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.630
Good point.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:40.050
But drinking sake among the 
autumn leaves is so elegant.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.760
By the way, drinking sake 
among autumn leaves

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.640
is a custom that dates back 
to the Tang Dynasty of China.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.020
I've gotta follow the group's example

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.430
and learn how to reach new frontiers

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.650
beyond my own boundaries...

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.150
Meanwhile, in France...

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.450
So this is Paris?

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.160
There are a lot of Japanese people.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.740
Let's find our hotel first.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.780
Yeah.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:10.250
Where is the Ritz Paris, that Hasegawa-san

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.000
is staying in, anyway?

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.120
Beats me.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.920
Yuuki 
Liquors

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.170
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.170
Yuuki 
Liquors

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.680
The Best of Sake 2012

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.680
Top Sake Choices

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:28.560
Sawaki will probably get 
a stomach ache.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.100
I should've sent some medicine with him.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.230
Merci.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:36.440
Damn it!

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.860
These French people only 
talk to us with a smile

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.570
when they want to bum a smoke!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.200
They're picking on you because 
you're wearing that shirt.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.700
Are you stupid?!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.200
This is my warning to the French!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:51.120
I'm physically expressing 
that France is lame

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.120
because it passes itself 
off as fashionable,

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.210
but still sells this lame crap everywhere!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.670
Who's going to pick up on that?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.960
They'll just think you're 
some foreign yokel.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:03.300
You know, I always 
imagined French cuisine

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.220
as small servings on small plates.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.510
So why does it feel like they're saying,

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.300
"Just try to eat all this, punk!"

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.810
You can say that again.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.230
I never expected servings this big.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.230
And everything tastes salty 
and comes with fries.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.150
It's just like America.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:24.240
But maybe wine is cheaper in France.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:25.780
Yeah, maybe.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.450
The glasses and utensils 
aren't too formal,

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.410
and from the size of the plates,

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.370
this seems to be your average 
popular restaurant.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:37.370
Not the kind of restaurant a rich 
girl like Hasegawa would frequent.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.760
Forty thousand for three people?!

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:48.890
At least the price lived 
up to my image of France.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.260
S-So cold...

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:53.270
And there aren't even any vacant taxis.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:57.140
Maybe we should've had someone 
call one from the restaurant.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:01.610
I know we've been waiting 
here for an hour,

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.320
but no customers are coming, either.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.280
Let's look for the subway.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:09.240
No, I can't take this cold anymore.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.490
Let's go in a café and 
have them call a cab.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.380
What'd he say?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:24.300
He said this is the tunnel where 
Princess Diana's car crashed.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.800
Anyway, we're definitely getting 
further away from the hotel.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.470
Is he picking on us?! He is, isn't he?!

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.260
Because we were all excited 
when we got a cab?!

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.770
It's all because of that 
stupid shirt of yours!

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:36.600
Take it off!

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.020
That has nothing to do with it!

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.940
Hey, mister, we don't need the tour! 
Take us to the hotel!

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.730
I'm not paying you!

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:45.820
It's tiny!

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.320
This is smaller than 
business hotels in Tokyo!

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.360
It really is small.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.490
Three people in a twin room...

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.830
Even if we use it normally, 
this is pretty tiny.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:58.830
I bet Hasegawa-san is 
staying in a nice place.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.340
So, we'll have to really start looking

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:05.670
for Hasegawa-san tomorrow...

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.180
Hasegawa? What are you talking about?

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.680
We came here to buy cheese and wine.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:15.140
Man, I'm tired.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.060
How is this city supposed to 
be number one in the world?

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.740
I wonder if things

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:30.070
have calmed down in the 
malt cellar by now...

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:36.950
Let's eat quick and get 
to Champs-Élysées.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.700
Who cares about streets?

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:41.000
As long as we're in Paris, 
we've gotta hit the museums.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.710
No, the streets! 
It's the streets that make Paris!

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:45.210
No, you guys...

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.710
What do we do about Hasegawa-san?

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:52.760
I told you, Itsuki only asked 
us to buy cheese and wine.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.220
Think of something fun 
you want to do, Sawaki.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.770
Champs-Élysées is straight ahead.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:08.820
What's that smell?

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.740
Cheese shops really smell...

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.370
France is the home of cheese, after all.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.740
It must taste amazing.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.250
Wow, so many of them...

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.000
I can't even see the cheese.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.380
You know, let's buy it on the way home.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.420
I don't know which ones would be good.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:31.510
Yeah.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.270
Foie gras carpaccio?!

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.480
All we're doing is eating.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.600
It's fine.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.940
We don't get to come here every day.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.610
How could we not enjoy all 
the flavors of Paris?

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.230
Wait, I've never had foie gras before!

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:52.030
Isn't it expensive?

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.740
Relax. It's a luxury in Japan,

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:56.620
but here, everyone eats it.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:06.920
Kawahama-san, is something wrong?

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.920
Did you eat too much? Pick up the pace!

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.670
No... sorry to spring this on you...

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:14.930
but we can't use much more money.

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:17.590
Why?!

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:20.720
So the foie gras <i>was</i> expensive?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.810
Sort of...

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.640
For real?! You said it was cheap!

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.480
That everyone eats it in Paris!

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.440
Shut up!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.520
It's because we've been 
drinking wine with every meal!

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.940
At this rate, by the day after 
tomorrow, we'll be living on water.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.700
There's no other way.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.950
There's only one thing 
we can rely on now.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:46.080
Place Vendôme 

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.250
Who thought we'd have to start

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:46.120
looking for Hasegawa by the second day?

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.960
We have no choice. 
Necessity knows no law.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.970
That was nerve-wracking...

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.970
How'd it go, Sawaki?

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:58.590
Leave it to the Ritz.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.140
I was able to speak in Japanese.

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:00.970
Really?

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:05.060
Your first "Bonjour" ended up 
being pointless, eh, Tadayasu?

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:05.980
Shut up.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.150
And what about Hasegawa?

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.730
They said she's been out 
since this morning.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.980
They wouldn't tell me anything else.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.950
Leave it to the Ritz.

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:20.990
Paris - Gare de Lyon

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.450
She'll come back eventually 
if we wait...

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.370
No, rich people stake out

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:28.620
a base in Paris and hang around there.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.290
Which means we'll freeze to death here?

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.500
We already checked out of the hotel...

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:38.430
All we can do is use Mutou-san's 
information to track Hasegawa-san down.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:42.510
Bringing Hasegawa back 
doesn't matter to us.

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:46.520
But it's true that we've got 
something to do for her now, too.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.310
Here, Sawaki.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.020
What's this?

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.610
It's Hasegawa's lab coat.

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.990
We couldn't do it, but maybe you'll be

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:01.030
able to pick up a little of her scent.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.530
I can see microbes, not scents!

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:08.580
Well, it's the only support 
we can offer now.

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:11.540
You can figure out the rest yourself.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:15.750
You're the one who dragged 
us here in the first place.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:18.050
Okay.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:22.340
Then let's start by heading 
south, to Burgundy.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:33.340
Ça va? We're about 370 kilometers 
west of Paris.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.630
Haruka-san, come look!

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:44.070
We're so high up, 
the people look like ants!

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:47.040
Uh... Haruka-san?

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:54.080
<i>More than a bird in a cage,</i>

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:58.460
<i>even more than prison...</i>

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.600
A monastery, huh?

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:12.560
It just looks like a fortress to me...

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Moyashimon

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Episode 7

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe 
Theater

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:58.150
P. chrysogenum

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:56.870
Stay away from the ducts!

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:58.150
You'll get ventilated!

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:00.350
The seats are too clean!

00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:01.020
A. alternata

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:01.800
Cling to a human!

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:05.370
Even an airplane flying 
through the stratosphere

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:07.390
is full of microbes.

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:09.620
Hey, look outside!

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:11.560
Wh-Who are you?

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:15.400
We're Deinococcus radiodurans!

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:23.300
D. radiodurans

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:17.760
We rode the dust all the way up here!

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:21.520
We can repair our own 
DNA when it's damaged,

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.320
so we can exist even 
in the stratosphere!

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:24.800
Wow...

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:28.490
We microbes can live not 
only in the stratosphere...

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:31.180
B. subtilis

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:31.180
E. carotovora

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:31.180
X. campestris

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:31.180
T. harzianum

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:31.180
E. cloacae

00:22:28.870 --> 00:22:30.320
but deep underground, too.

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:33.320
There are even some that

00:22:33.320 --> 00:22:37.080
love to live in undersea volcanic vents!

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:44.150
T. thermophilus

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:42.230
Hello, I'm Thermus thermophilus and 
I love undersea volcanic vents!

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:44.610
By the way, we were discovered in...

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:46.990
Izu Hot Spring

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:47.390
a hot spring in Izu!

00:22:47.390 --> 00:22:50.790
The world of microbes 
is endless! Amazing!
